# The original asset drops, verbatim: 24 MB of mostly .mp4/.gif turntables and
# animation reels. The useful subset is extracted into assets/, docs/, tools/
# and reference/ and IS tracked; these are the provenance record, not a build
# input, and putting them in git history would cost more than they are worth.
# See README.md's "What came from where".
archives/

# Raw audio drops: ~280 MB of source stems and jukebox material that the
# build never reads. Same reasoning as archives/ above — provenance, not a
# build input. The files the ROM actually consumes are tracked:
#   assets/music/petabyte.mid          -> the XM64 score
#   assets/music/petabyte_theme.mp3    -> the streamed recording
#   assets/music/ostafterstart.mp3     -> the narration crawl's score
assets/music/*
!assets/music/petabyte.mid
!assets/music/petabyte_theme.mp3
!assets/music/ostafterstart.mp3
